WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.145
Pinocchio swam hard through the waves.

2
00:00:03.146 --> 00:00:05.919
Because he was made of wood, he floated.

3
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.652
But the waves threw him all around.

4
00:00:08.653 --> 00:00:12.673
Geppetto’s boat was still far away.

5
00:00:12.674 --> 00:00:17.804
"I’ll never reach Geppetto’s boat in time!" Pinocchio cried.

6
00:00:17.805 --> 00:00:21.520
His mouth was full of salt water, and his arms were getting tired.

7
00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.279
But he kept swimming.

8
00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.267
To the side, he saw a small island.

9
00:00:26.268 --> 00:00:31.085
He swam to it so he could rest.

10
00:00:31.086 --> 00:00:35.206
While Pinocchio sat on the island, he looked for Geppetto’s boat.

11
00:00:35.207 --> 00:00:37.980
"Oh, Father . . . where are you?

12
00:00:37.981 --> 00:00:41.164
Wait, I see you!

13
00:00:41.165 --> 00:00:44.923
There is a whale by your boat . . . and . . . oh!

14
00:00:44.924 --> 00:00:47.322
The whale ate your boat!"

15
00:00:47.323 --> 00:00:50.818
Pinocchio could not see Geppetto anymore.

16
00:00:50.819 --> 00:00:53.274
He thought Geppetto had drowned.

17
00:00:53.275 --> 00:00:56.758
"Oh, Father! I didn’t save you!

18
00:00:56.759 --> 00:01:03.465
I am so sorry. Whaaa!" Pinocchio cried.

19
00:01:03.466 --> 00:01:05.818
Just then, it started to rain.

20
00:01:05.819 --> 00:01:08.325
"Oh, I need to get dry.

21
00:01:08.326 --> 00:01:11.379
Father would want me to be safe and dry,"

22
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:16.860
Pinocchio said, and he ran into the nearby village.

23
00:01:16.861 --> 00:01:21.094
"Please, sir," he said to a man walking by with a coal cart.

24
00:01:21.095 --> 00:01:25.099
"May I stay at your house, where it’s dry?"

25
00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:31.235
"If you help me carry this coal, you may stay with me tonight," the man answered.

26
00:01:31.236 --> 00:01:36.488
"Oh, I don’t want to carry coal!" Pinocchio said, offended.

27
00:01:36.489 --> 00:01:42.466
He wanted the man to help him without having to work.

28
00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:44.238
It rained harder.

29
00:01:44.239 --> 00:01:51.779
"Please, ma’am," he said to a woman carrying water jugs, "may I stay at your house where it’s dry?"

30
00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:57.930
"If you help me carry these jugs, you may stay with me tonight."

31
00:01:57.931 --> 00:02:01.255
Pinocchio didn’t want to carry the water jugs.

32
00:02:01.256 --> 00:02:04.382
But he wanted to be dry, so he agreed.

33
00:02:04.383 --> 00:02:08.227
The jugs were very heavy, but Pinocchio didn’t complain.

34
00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:13.522
He carried them all the way to the woman’s small house.

35
00:02:13.523 --> 00:02:16.188
Once inside, he sat down.

36
00:02:16.189 --> 00:02:17.861
"Here are the jugs.

37
00:02:17.862 --> 00:02:20.498
Thank you for letting me stay."

38
00:02:20.499 --> 00:02:23.692
"You are welcome," the woman said.

39
00:02:23.693 --> 00:02:29.456
"A little work never hurt anyone. Right, Pinocchio?"

40
00:02:29.457 --> 00:02:35.067
"How do you know my name?" he asked, surprised.

41
00:02:35.068 --> 00:02:39.748
The woman lifted her hood, and out fell her pretty blue hair.

42
00:02:39.749 --> 00:02:42.941
"Oh, Blue Fairy! It’s you!

43
00:02:42.942 --> 00:02:45.317
But, why did you make me work?

44
00:02:45.318 --> 00:02:48.654
Why didn’t you help me?" Pinocchio asked.

45
00:02:48.655 --> 00:02:51.511
"I did help you, Pinocchio.

46
00:02:51.512 --> 00:02:55.272
It is a good thing to get help from strangers.

47
00:02:55.273 --> 00:02:59.530
But it is an even better thing to help strangers.

48
00:02:59.531 --> 00:03:02.681
I wanted you to learn that lesson.

49
00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:07.082
Did you follow the road home as I showed you?" she asked.

50
00:03:07.083 --> 00:03:10.705
"I tried to follow the road," Pinocchio said.

51
00:03:10.706 --> 00:03:15.656
"But, I got trapped and then flown and then I swam.

52
00:03:15.657 --> 00:03:21.226
And when I stopped swimming, I saw Father get eaten by a whale!"

53
00:03:21.227 --> 00:03:25.404
As soon as Pinocchio said this, he started to cry.

54
00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:27.775
"Do not cry, Pinocchio.

55
00:03:27.776 --> 00:03:31.472
Your father is safe, but he is hidden.

56
00:03:31.473 --> 00:03:35.421
I will help you find him," said the Blue Fairy.

57
00:03:35.422 --> 00:03:37.384
"Father is alive?

58
00:03:37.385 --> 00:03:40.750
We should leave right now!" Pinocchio said.

59
00:03:40.751 --> 00:03:43.827
"No, Geppetto is safe.

60
00:03:43.828 --> 00:03:47.041
First, we must eat dinner and get some sleep.

61
00:03:47.042 --> 00:03:49.900
We will be stronger tomorrow."

62
00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:54.454
"I wish I were bigger and stronger," Pinocchio said.

63
00:03:54.455 --> 00:03:58.693
"If I were bigger and stronger, I could have saved Father.

64
00:03:58.694 --> 00:04:01.493
But, I’m only a piece of wood.

65
00:04:01.494 --> 00:04:05.833
I wish I were a real boy who could grow into a man."

66
00:04:05.834 --> 00:04:13.847
"Perhaps, if you are a good boy who obeys his father, you will become a real boy someday.

67
00:04:13.848 --> 00:04:16.672
But now, you must sleep, Pinocchio.

68
00:04:16.673 --> 00:04:23.038
We have a big day ahead of us tomorrow."

